<p class="ltx_p">The double series and double product are absolutely and uniformly convergent in
compact sets in <math class="ltx_Math" altimg="m20.png" altimg-height="18px" altimg-valign="-2px" altimg-width="19px" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline"><mi href="./front/introduction#common.t1.r1" title="complex plane">ℂ</mi></math> that do not include lattice points. Hence the order
of the terms or factors is immaterial.</p>
</div>
<div id="ii.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p class="ltx_p">When <math class="ltx_Math" altimg="m63.png" altimg-height="21px" altimg-valign="-3px" altimg-width="54px" alttext="z\notin\mathbb{L}" display="inline"><mrow><mi href="./23.1#t1.r4" title="complex">z</mi><mo href="./front/introduction#common.t1.r11" title="not an element of">∉</mo><mi href="./23.1#t1.r1" title="lattice">𝕃</mi></mrow></math> the functions are related by</p>
